Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Native collection invocation through the new standard library (the locally-bound-map `:k` → 9 fixture) and bundled primitive shadowing of bare `get`/`assoc` (which otherwise resolve through the source store before VM primitives); unified `yang.clojure` suite green. The real `clj → clj.py → clj` cross-syntax unwind (cleanup + context restoration) gates ONLY at P3′, after `clj.py` exists. |\n   648\t| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` (the legacy `py-v1` descriptor pins today's `'py/*` hooks 1:1 — behavior-preserving, gated by the existing CPython oracle suites); publish `clj.py`; flip `yang.python`'s default `runtime-profile` to `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (a revision re-pin in `yang.frontend`). | py goldens regenerate under the descriptor-driven path (legacy descriptor byte-identical outcomes); clojure-core-v1 gets fresh goldens | Legacy-descriptor behavior preservation: full CPython corpus + 4-host parity under `py-v1` pin; end-to-end 4-host `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` suite (numeric/float ops, `:max-bits 53` limit traps, `data/admit-key?` refusals, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-entries` ordering, deterministic `str`/`gensym`); capability refusal tests (typed `except E:`, `genexpr` under `:control/generators :refused`); default-profile regressions (r8): an unqualified `:k` key admits successfully (the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only); equal exact integers in different host carriers hit the same map entry on insert AND lookup; a local/projected value equal to `:clj/unbound` remains distinguishable from an absent binding; canonical traversal order matches Jing encoded-byte order (`0` before `nil`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, unqualified hooks, reserved doors, out-of-closure exports. |\n   649\t| **P4′ — Additional N → 1 profiles** | `:yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1` next (descriptor + ts frontend contract); `:yang.php/clojure-core-v1` after. | Fresh goldens per profile | End-to-end parity suites per profile. |\n   650\t| **Track B — Legacy prelude re-architecture (deferred, on demand)** | Migrate the native `py`/`js`/`php` preludes onto `yrt.effect`/`yrt.int`/boxed float (the r6 P1/P4 legs: 4→5-slot contexts, generators via `:gen/yield`, `yrt.safepoint`, `php.sp` integration per its own hooks); undertaken only when legacy demand justifies it. | Refresh py/js/php goldens per migration slice | The r6 P1/P4 gates apply verbatim at that time, attached here by value: generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup and Python `:base` rebasing; migration of `py`/`js`/`php` onto `yrt.effect`, `yrt.int`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` (4→5-slot contexts; `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` for bundled `clj`); existing Python & PHP generator tests green; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n   651\t\n   652\t---\n   653\t\n   654\t## 10. Owner decisions and disposition ledger\n   655\t\n   656\t1. **D10 — Default-profile policy & legacy-track deferral (`Settled — r7 Owner Directive`):** For the parameterized frontends, the **Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` first; ts/php to follow); the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist at their current content addresses with passing oracle suites), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to Track B until legacy demand justifies it. The clojure prelude family is built first. Consequence named in §6.1: capability refusals (classes, generators, typed `except`, `with`, kwargs) are the default experience for source written against native semantics; pinning the legacy revision is the escape hatch.\n   657\t2. **D1 — Local mutation model for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`:**\n   658\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `:mutation/locals :cell` (task-heap cells holding pure persistent Clojure values, matching Python parameter binding, unbound reads, reassignment, loops, and `nonlocal` with per-module `globals` cells). Keep `:single-assignment` as a separate restricted profile.\n   659\t   - *Option B:* `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` only (refuses local reassignment).\n   660\t2. **D2 — Namespace prefix for Layer-2a shared modules:**\n   661\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `yrt.*` (`yrt.effect`, `yrt.int`, `yrt.safepoint`) matching `yang.typescript.md` §17 and `yang.php.md` §9, implemented in Clojure under `src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`.\n   662\t   - *Option B:* `yang.rt.*` for both Clojure namespaces and linker module names.\n   663\t3. **D3 — Python float tagging (r7: moot until Track B — py keeps its tagged `{:py/float}` representation as-frozen; boxed `yin.vm.float` ships for the Clojure path in P0′):**\n   664\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Retain `{:py/float x}` behind a 2-line `py` boundary adapter around boxed `yin.vm.float` through P1 so Python's `1 == 1.0` oracle semantics stay cleanly isolated.\n   665\t   - *Option B:* Migrate Python to untagged `data/float64` carriers in P1.\n   666\t4. **D4 — Golden migration policy (`Settled — Owner Clean-Slate Directive`):**\n   667\t   - Settled in favor of clean golden regeneration per slice (`P0`–`P4`), preserving correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and language-oracle suites rather than frozen-quirk backwards compatibility.\n   668\t5. **D5 — Cross-syntax identifier mapping for Clojure names (`?`, `!`, `-`):**\n   669\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Curated `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` table validated against UAST-derived arity/roles, unit-bound `ambient-resolver`, lexical precedence, and reserved-door bans (`*.impl/*`, `dsg__*`).\n   670\t   - *Option B:* Algorithmic mangling rule (`_q` / `_bang`).\n   671\t6. **D6 — Publishing `clojure.core` and migrating `yang.clojure` (`Settled — Owner Clean-Slate Directive`):**\n   672\t   - Settled in favor of publishing collision-free `clojure.core.impl` + cell-free `clojure.core` AND migrating `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core` in P3 (retiring `yang.clojure`'s legacy `library-for` duplication and unit-local `dsg__call_token` path).\n   673\t7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (r7: `fpow-half` ships in P0′ for the Clojure path; `fpow-base` defers to Track B with the php re-architecture):**\n   674\t   - *Option A (Recommended for P0/P1 — Architect concurred):* Export both `float/fpow-half` and `float/fpow-base` in `yin.vm.float` so `1.1 ** 6` preserves bit-exact parity (`0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across existing CPython/Node and PHP language oracles.\n   675\t   - *Option B:* Explicitly approve unifying PHP onto `fpow-half` (or `py`/`js` onto `fpow-base`) and update the affected language's oracle departure ledger.\n   676\t8. **D8 — Three-tier hybrid architecture (`Settled — r6 Owner Directive`):**\n   677\t   - Settled on: (1) `:pure` host value core (`yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.integer`, boxed `yin.vm.float`, `kind/namespace`) for total, representation-sensitive ops; (2) unified guest algebraic effects (`yrt.effect` over `%capture`) for control flow, generators, and cold error/limit policy traps; (3) minimal VM/stream effects (`cell/*`, `stream/*`, `:module/require`) per ADR 0004.\n   678\t9. **D9 — Focused swappable-prelude scope (`Settled — r6 Owner Directive`):**\n   679\t   - Settled on supporting **Native profiles** (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`) for existing language code plus **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profiles** (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`, future `:yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1`), omitting unnecessary off-diagonal N×M profiles (such as `:yang.clojure/py-v1`) and keeping `yang.clojure` directly on unified `clj` + `clojure.core`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
