{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'handler contract|underlying VM effects|policy tags|declared footprint|first non-|gate.*cross|cross-syntax|capture and restore|left fold' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | cut -c1-1300\"","aggregated_output":"15:- **2026-11-21 (r7 → r8 reconciliation):** Addressed all findings from the r7 architect review (thread `01a1faa3-bb7e-7c30-b3bf-cedbad008bfc`; 8 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, plus default-profile regressions): (H1) explicit default-selector mechanism — the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[id revision]`, applied at the normal request entry, with two-revision / legacy-pin / in-flight-snapshot gates; (H2) per-frontend **entry-lowering contracts** emitting the landed native entry shapes (`py` 1-arg `run-main`, `js` 1-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with request stream) alongside the Clojure resolver-bearing 2-arg shape; (H3) ONE derivation record (frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output), pins reconciled by module symbol before lowering, dependency-first installation in linked composition, resolver derivation in provenance / live cell in the task; (H4) complete effect-unwind traversal per frame kind with exactly-once cleanup, a P2′ cold-error policy for plain `yang.clojure`, `clojure.core.impl` owning zero cells while declaring its runtime effects; (H5) address-bound export-**role** evidence (same-arity wrong-role fails closed); (H6) the §5.1 example labeled a Track B recipe recording bundled shape, linked trailing forms, pins, an\n205:- **Unwind traversal semantics (r8):** `raise` delivers to the first non-`:finally` boundary; on the way down every `:finally` frame runs its cleanup closure **exactly once**, and every `:effect` frame is popped with its context restored (an `:effect` frame carries no cleanup closure — a guest throw crossing an unrelated effect handler is a plain unwind past it, never an error). `perform` walks `ctx-cell` to the nearest matching `:effect` frame **without** running `:finally` frames; only when the handler aborts without resuming does the abort path run the traversed `:finally` cleanups during that unwind. In all cases the context is restored to the surviving frame's state and each cleanup runs at most once per activation.\n309:6. **Dual-emitter standardization & Parity Law:** Standardized linked emission applies to the **P0′ Clojure-family modules** (`:trailing-requires []`, `:finalize-c1? true`) — it does NOT retroactively standardize the frozen native preludes (r8: landed `py` ends its module tree with `require yang.call` and has no C1 finalizer there; php likewise; the bundled clojure continuation family is a left fold — the `:mode` field alone cannot freeze these, so each frozen runtime records its bundled shape, linked trailing forms, dependency pins, and C1 side-table identity-or-absence **independently**). Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n573:   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells — but it DECLARES its runtime effects**: the `:coll/unsupported-key` and `:int/*` effects its definitions perform are part of its declared footprint, installed by the owning entry's policy handlers — `clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n646:| **P1′ — `yrt.effect` + `yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers; unified trusted `clj`** | Implement stateless `yrt.effect` (5-slot `data/nth` frames, abortive `raise`/`try-value`/`try-orelse`/`try-finally`/`call-ec`, plus resumable `handle`/`perform` — the 